<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Crohn disease of the terminal ileum and colon (ileocolitis), Montreal A2 L3 B1 without perianal disease, moderate to severe: deep ileal ulcers over 15 cm and patchy colonic ulcers, SES-CD 14, Harvey-Bradshaw Index 11; intestinal tuberculosis excluded by negative interferon-gamma release assay, normal chest X-ray, and biopsies negative for acid-fast bacilli, TB PCR, and mycobacterial culture; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to her documented chronic intestinal illness, whose historical diagnosis is not settled</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>K50.80</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis confirmed within the modern episode; her historical illness is documented (D), but whether it was intestinal tuberculosis or Crohn disease remains a retrospective interpretation (R) and is disputed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Four months of crampy right lower abdominal pain, loose stools up to six times a day including at night, low-grade evening fevers, and loss of 6 kg; inflammatory markers raised; colonoscopy and small-bowel imaging booked</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R19.7</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the diagnosis; the documented symptoms of early 1915 are echoed (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Iron deficiency anemia from chronic intestinal blood loss and poor absorption (hemoglobin 10.6 g/dL, MCV 76, ferritin 9)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D50.0</td><td>S — Synthetic finding at presentation; corrected by intravenous iron.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Moderate protein-calorie malnutrition: BMI 17.6 after losing 6 kg (12 percent of body weight) in four months; albumin 3.3 g/dL</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E44.0</td><td>S — Synthetic nutritional status at presentation; resolved with treatment and dietitian support.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Vitamin D deficiency (25-hydroxyvitamin D 18 ng/mL)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E55.9</td><td>S — Synthetic finding at presentation.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

  <entry typeCode="DRIV">
